Third-party notices

Training attention, model-forward, collation, video, and position utilities are
adapted from ThinkStream (Thinking in Streaming Video), CASIA-IVA-Lab.
Its MIT copyright and permission notice are preserved in LICENSE.

Model support uses Qwen through Hugging Face Transformers and Liger Kernel;
video preprocessing uses qwen-vl-utils and PyAV. Dependencies retain their own licenses.
No model weights or dependency source distributions are bundled.

sF1 implements the GuideMe temporal–semantic matching protocol; gF1 and PQS
follow PWR. The PQS judging rubric is provided with its evaluation driver.
